['**`complete(id, token, result)`** records the result. Throws `StaleLeaseError` if the lease is no longer yours. RFC 007 changes what this returns.',
 '**`complete(id, token, result)`** commits the result and returns a receipt `{ id, outcome, token, result, completedAt, completionSeq }`. `outcome` is `committed` the first time and `already-committed` for a repeat with the same token (nothing is written, and the stored result is returned). Any other token throws `StaleLeaseError`; a pruned job throws `UnknownJobError`. The call returns once the record is on disk. See [RFC 007](rfc-007-exactly-once-completion.md).\n\n**`getResult(id)`** returns `{ id, status: \'done\', result, token, attempts, completedAt, completionSeq }` for a finished job, `{ id, status }` for any other, and `null` for an unknown or pruned one.\n\n**`completions({ after, limit })`** returns the retained commits in commit order, `[{ seq, id, token, result, completedAt }]`, with `seq > after`. Numbers start at 1 and never repeat or go back, across restarts and compaction.\n\n**`reclaimWorker(workerId, { reason })`** gives up every lease held by a worker known to be dead, at once and with no backoff, and returns `[{ id, status }]` (`ready`, or `dead` when attempts have run out). The attempt counts, `reason` becomes `lastError`, and the old tokens are stale.'],
['`WalqError` is the base class. `CorruptLogError` has an `offset`. Also `StaleLeaseError`, `UnknownJobError`, `LockTimeoutError`, `InvalidTransitionError`, `ConfigError`, `QueueClosedError`.',
 '`WalqError` is the base class. `CorruptLogError` has an `offset`. Also `StaleLeaseError`, `UnknownJobError`, `LockTimeoutError`, `InvalidTransitionError`, `ConfigError`, `QueueClosedError`, and `RecordTooLargeError` (a record would not fit in a 64 MiB frame; nothing was written).'],
['- `start()` starts the workers.', 'Worker ids are unique across pools and processes. When the pool sees a worker exit it reclaims that worker\'s leases at once (`reclaimWorker`) and starts a replacement, so a killed worker\'s job does not wait for its lease.\n\n- `start()` starts the workers.'],
['`message` carries worker events (`kind` is one of `ready`, `job-started`, `job-completed`, `job-failed`, `job-fenced`, `worker-error`)', '`message` carries worker events (`kind` is one of `ready`, `job-started`, `job-completed`, `job-failed`, `job-fenced`, `worker-error`). A worker that has finished a job keeps trying to record the outcome until it is recorded or the worker learns it was fenced (`job-fenced`)'],
]);
